libdvdnav: keep SPRM 14 as the player set it.

SPRM 14 is the player's display configuration (its aspect and output
mode), which a disc's commands read to choose menus and pictures.
vm_get_video_aspect() overwrote its aspect bits with the content's aspect
on every call, so a player on a 4:3 display claimed 16:9 as soon as a
16:9 title was asked about. It now only returns the content's aspect.

--- a/src/vm/vmget.c
+++ b/src/vm/vmget.c
@@ -300,9 +300,8 @@
     return -1;
   }
 
-  (vm->state).registers.SPRM[14] &= ~(0x3 << 10);
-  (vm->state).registers.SPRM[14] |= aspect << 10;
-
+  /* SPRM 14 is the player's display, which discs read; the content's aspect
+     is returned, not written there. */
   return aspect;
 }
 
